# Block A — Opponent Model: Implementation Plan

## Background & Goal

This plan covers the design and implementation of the **F1 SIS Opponent Model**, which produces calibrated per-lap probabilities `P(PIT | state_t)` and `P(STAY | state_t)` for each opponent. These probabilities feed directly into the Monte Carlo Strategy Engine.

The plan is grounded in a complete inspection of the existing codebase. All model interfaces and data schemas described here reflect what actually exists — no outputs have been invented.

---

## TASK 1 — Foundational Model Inspection

### 1A. Lap-Time Model ([`lap_time/adapter.py`](file:///c:/Roshith/Projects/F1-SIS/src/lap_time/adapter.py))

**Model type:** scikit-learn regressor (loaded from `laptime_model.pkl`)  
**Training data:** 2018–2024 races (from `f1_consolidated_data.csv` and per-race CSVs)

**Inputs (15 features):**

| Feature | Description | Unit |
|---|---|---|
| `Track_encoded` | LabelEncoded circuit | int |
| `Team_encoded` | LabelEncoded constructor | int |
| `LapNumber` | Absolute race lap | int |
| `TyreLife` | Tyre age | laps |
| `tyre_age_squared` | Non-linear degradation proxy | laps² |
| `Compound_HARD/MEDIUM/SOFT` | One-hot compound flags | binary |
| `fuel_load` | 110 × (1 − lap/total) | kg |
| `race_progress_pct` | lap/total × 100 | % |
| `stint_number` | Stint index | int |
| `is_fresh_tyre` | Was tyre new at start of stint | binary |
| `Position` | Current race position | int |
| `fuel_tyre_interaction` | (fuel_load/110) × tyre_life | composite |
| `Event_Dry_Base` | Calibrated circuit dry lap baseline | seconds |

**Outputs:**

- `predict_lap_time(state, driver)` → `float` (seconds) — predicted total dry lap time
- `predict_all(state)` → `dict[driver_code → float]` (seconds) — batch for all active drivers
- Internal: predicts `delta_from_dry_base`; final = `Event_Dry_Base + delta`
- Includes **dynamic calibration** from observed clean green-flag laps

**Horizon:** current lap (single-lap prediction, not multi-lap rollout)  
**Can apply to opponent:** ✅ Yes — `predict_lap_time(state, opponent_code)` works for any driver in the state  
**Predicts future lap time:** ❌ Not directly. It predicts expected pace for the **current lap's conditions** (tyre age, compound, lap number). You can approximate `t+k` by incrementing `TyreLife` and `LapNumber` manually.  
**Pace relative to another car:** ❌ Not built in, but derivable: `predict_lap_time(state, opp) - predict_lap_time(state, ego)`  
**Uncertainty:** ❌ No prediction intervals from this model (point estimate only)  
**Wet/Intermediate:** Returns `None` — model is dry-compound only

