### 1B. Tyre Degradation Model ([`tyre_deg/adapter.py`](file:///c:/Roshith/Projects/F1-SIS/src/tyre_deg/adapter.py))

**Model type:** XGBoost regressor (`xgboost_baseline.json`)  
**Target:** `Target_Tyre_Degradation` = pure tyre-degradation pace deficit (seconds) relative to fuel-corrected benchmark  
**Test performance:** MAE = 0.423 s/lap, RMSE = 0.712 s/lap, R² = 0.844 (2025 holdout)

**Inputs (12 features):**

| Feature | Description | Unit |
|---|---|---|
| `TyreAge` | Tyre age (laps) | laps |
| `Log_TyreAge` | log1p(TyreAge) | — |
| `StintLap` | Laps since last pit + 1 | laps |
| `Compound_Encoded` | Ordinal: SOFT=1, MEDIUM=2, HARD=3 | int |
| `RaceProgressFraction` | current_lap / total_laps | [0,1] |
| `TrackTemp` | Track surface temperature | °C |
| `AirTemp` | Ambient air temperature | °C |
| `is_safety_car` | SC deployed this lap | binary |
| `is_vsc` | VSC deployed this lap | binary |
| `Lag1_Pace_Residual` | Pace residual from 1 lap ago | seconds |
| `Rolling3_Degradation_Trend` | Linear slope of last 3-lap residuals | s/lap |
| `Team_Median_Pace_Lag1` | Team historical pace prior | seconds |

**Outputs:**

- `predict_degradation(state, driver)` → `float` (seconds) — pure tyre degradation component
- `predict_all(state)` → `dict[driver_code → float]` — batch
- `predict_lap_time(state, driver)` → `float` — `base + fuel_penalty + degradation`
- `observe_lap(state)` — call every lap boundary to update internal residual history

**Compounds supported:** SOFT, MEDIUM, HARD (wet/inter return valid values but are mechanically excluded from the model's meaningful range)  
**Tyre-age dependency:** ✅ Explicit via `TyreAge` and `Log_TyreAge`; `Rolling3_Degradation_Trend` captures acceleration of degradation  
**Uncertainty:** ❌ Point estimate only  
**Can apply to opponent:** ✅ Yes — works for any driver in state  
**Future degradation:** ❌ Not directly. Can approximate by advancing `TyreAge` manually.

