### 1C. Safety Car / Race-State Model ([`sc_risk/adapter.py`](file:///c:/Roshith/Projects/F1-SIS/src/sc_risk/adapter.py) + `SC_Risk_Estimation.ipynb`)

**Model type:** Logistic Regression hazard model (primary), XGBoost with Platt calibration (higher-horizon)  
**Training seasons:** 2018–2023  **Validation:** 2024  **Test:** 2025  

**`SCRiskAdapter.build_H_t(state)`** produces an 8-feature dict:

| Feature | Description | Unit |
|---|---|---|
| `logit_p_sc_hist` | Logit of historical SC rate for this circuit × progress bin | logit |
| `logit_p_vsc_hist` | Logit of historical VSC rate for this circuit × progress bin | logit |
| `close_battles` | Count of gaps < 1 s between adjacent cars | count |
| `field_spread` | Std dev of gap-to-leader across field | seconds |
| `sector_anomaly_score` | Max sector slowdown vs. rolling median (anomaly signal) | fraction |
| `recent_retirements` | New retirements in last 3 laps | count |
| `yellow_last3` | Sum of yellow-flag laps in last 3 laps | count |
| `sc_count_cumul` | Cumulative SC deployments so far in race | count |

**`get_fcy_probabilities(H_t, logit_sc, logit_vsc, X_sc, X_vsc)`** returns:

```python
{
    'SC':  {1: 0.03, 3: 0.08, 5: 0.14, 10: 0.25},   # P(SC within n laps)
    'VSC': {1: 0.02, 3: 0.06, 5: 0.10, 10: 0.18},
}
```

**Horizons:** 1, 3, 5, 10 laps  
**Transition probabilities:** ❌ Not modelled (no state machine; each call is independent)  
**Per-driver output:** ❌ Field-level only — SC/VSC probability applies to the entire race, not a specific opponent  
**Can apply to opponent:** Partially — SC probability affects all drivers equally; it doesn't predict an individual opponent's strategic response to SC  
**Uncertainty representation:** Calibrated probabilities via Platt scaling  
**Leakage note:** Training seasons 2018–2023; validation 2024; test 2025. ✅ No leakage if Opponent Model test races ⊆ 2025.

