## TASK 2 — Training-Data Unit

Each sample is:

$$\text{Sample}_{i,r,t} = (\text{Driver } i, \text{ Race } r, \text{ Lap } t)$$

The **target** is what driver `i` does on lap `t+1`:

$$y_{i,r,t} = \mathbf{1}(\text{driver } i \text{ pits on lap } t+1)$$

**Pit detection:** A row has `PitInTimeSeconds` populated if the driver pitted at the end of that lap. Formally:

```python
target = 1 if df.loc[(driver, lap+1), 'PitInTimeSeconds'].notna() else 0
```

All features must come exclusively from laps ≤ t.

