| 2018 | 20 | TRAIN |
| 2019 | 21 | TRAIN |
| 2020 | 17 | TRAIN |
| 2021 | 22 | TRAIN |
| 2022 | 22 | TRAIN |
| 2023 | 22 | TRAIN |
| 2024 | 24 | VALIDATION |
| 2025 | 24 | TEST |

**Rationale:**
- Season-level split preserves race-level separation naturally.
- Matches the SC model's split: trained 2018–2023, validated 2024, tested 2025 — eliminates foundational-model leakage entirely.
- 2020 data is included but flagged: COVID calendar had no fans and fewer races; may exhibit anomalous strategy behaviour.
- Total ~128 train races × ~14 drivers × ~45 clean laps/driver ≈ **~80,000 training samples** (rough estimate before exclusions).

> [!IMPORTANT]
> All rows from a single race must remain in the same split. No random row-level shuffling.

