## TASK 11 — Probability Calibration

**Why:** XGBoost pit probabilities are often overconfident (pushed toward 0 or 1). The Monte Carlo engine needs calibrated probabilities.

**Methods to compare:**
1. Raw XGBoost probabilities
2. Platt scaling (sigmoid fitting on validation set)
3. Isotonic regression (on validation set)

**Calibration is fitted on the validation set (2024) only.** The calibrated model is evaluated on test (2025).

**Calibration metrics:**
- Brier Score
- Log Loss
- ECE (10 equal-width bins, [0,1])
- MCE (maximum bin error)
- Reliability diagram (predicted probability vs. observed frequency)

