## TASK 12–18 — Evaluation Metrics

All metrics computed on test set (2025 races), never used for model selection.

### Classification

- Accuracy, Precision, Recall, F1 (PIT class primary)
- ROC-AUC
- Confusion matrix
- PIT precision, PIT recall, STAY precision, STAY recall

### Probability Quality

- Brier Score: $BS = \frac{1}{N}\sum(p_i - y_i)^2$
- Log Loss
- Probability MAE: $\frac{1}{N}\sum|p_i - y_i|$
- Probability RMSE: $\sqrt{\frac{1}{N}\sum(p_i-y_i)^2}$

### Action Error

$$\text{ActionError} = \frac{FP+FN}{N}$$
$$\text{FalsePITRate} = \frac{FP}{FP+TN}$$
$$\text{MissedPITRate} = \frac{FN}{FN+TP}$$

### Error Breakdown (Task 16)

Errors broken down by:
- Tyre age bins: [0–5], [6–10], [11–15], [16–20], [21+]
- Race phase: Early (0–33%), Middle (33–66%), Late (66–100%)
- Compound: Soft, Medium, Hard
- Track status: Normal, VSC, SC
- Predicted probability bins: [0–0.2], [0.2–0.4], [0.4–0.6], [0.6–0.8], [0.8–1.0]

### Driver-Level Error (Task 18)

Reported where driver has ≥ 50 PIT samples in the test set. Drivers with fewer are grouped as "Other".

