## TASK 22 — Engineering Targets

| Metric | Target | Basis |
|---|---|---|
| ROC-AUC | > 0.70 | Meaningful discrimination above random |
| Brier | < empirical baseline (≈ 0.0475) | Must outperform $p(PIT)=\text{const}$ |
| Log Loss | < empirical baseline | |
| ECE | < 0.05 | Required for reliable MC sampling |
| Probability MAE | < 0.20 | |
| Action Accuracy | > empirical baseline | |

**Empirical baseline Brier**: If $p(PIT) = 0.05$ always, $BS = 0.05 × (1-0.05)^2 + 0.95 × (0-0.05)^2 ≈ 0.0475$.

These are **development targets**, not scientific acceptance criteria. If the model does not meet them, investigate features rather than forcing the model.

