## Open Questions

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Q1: 2020 season anomaly.** The 2020 calendar was shortened and raced without fans. Should 2020 races be included in the training set, excluded entirely, or down-weighted?  
> **Recommendation for MVP:** Include but add a `year` feature to the model so it can learn season-level differences.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Q2: Wet/Intermediate exclusion.** Wet tyre laps are excluded because the LT model returns `None`. Should we:
> (a) Simply exclude all wet laps, or  
> (b) Build a separate wet-strategy indicator and keep the rows with imputed predictions?  
> **Recommendation for MVP:** Exclude wet laps. Extend later.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Q3: Bayesian lambda tuning.** The blending weight `λ` controls how much race-specific evidence overrides the ML prior. Should this be tuned as a global constant or per-compound?  
> **Recommendation for MVP:** Tune as a single global constant on validation set.

> [!NOTE]
> **Q4: Mandatory pit stops.** Some circuits require compound variety (at least one non-SC stop). Should the model learn the mandatory window or should it be enforced as a hard constraint downstream?  
> **Recommendation for MVP:** Let the model learn it from data (the pattern will appear in historical lap ages).

> [!NOTE]
> **Q5: Future t+1 approximation.** We approximate `predicted_lap_time_t1` by advancing `TyreAge+1` in the LT model. This is a simplification. Is this acceptable?  
> **Recommendation for MVP:** Yes — it provides a gradient signal for degradation acceleration without needing a separate forward-prediction model.

